  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fc7bebddc280debd4bde32393cabfa4a6a91a782d38e5406f374cc4eaa4ac68f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{\u2015}{{A}^{\u2032}{B}^{\u2032}},$ the image of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{\u2032}(5,7)$ and ${B}^{\u2032}(-9,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/177ca7f40ef24cf2f45a15b78487700d1f0efd094c975079cf4704b46debefb1.png)",
